# Maps each NetApp SVM (vserver) to the ONTAP REST API base URL to
# reach it on - the same data LIF already used for that SVM's
# NFS/CIFS backup traffic (management service enabled on it), not a
# separate cluster management LIF. One line per SVM, not per share:
# several shares/volumes commonly live on the same SVM and share one
# line here.
#
# "<SVM name>  <https://host-or-ip-of-that-SVM's-LIF>"
#
# The user/password used against every SVM's API is the same
# everywhere (NETAPP_API_USER/NETAPP_API_PASSWORD in secrets.env) -
# only the endpoint differs, which is what this file is for. If a
# given cluster instead uses a per-SVM password, this project doesn't
# support that yet - ask for it if you need it.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Copy to
# /etc/restic/netapp-svms.conf.

svm-cs3-bnl-dev     https://10.110.136.44
SVMCIGOUVZ1001      https://10.110.136.43
